  "howItWorks": "How does this work?",
  "howItWorksBody": "Each cycle length is modelled as a bell curve (Gaussian) with an unknown average and spread. Starting from typical values (about 28.5 ± 3.5 days), the app updates its belief with every gap between your logged dates using Bayes' rule. Gaps don't need to be consecutive: a 3-month gap is automatically recognised as about 3 cycles. Recent data counts more than old data.\n\nThe forecast mixes all plausible averages and spreads, so the uncertainty honestly grows for cycles further ahead. Not medical advice and not contraception.",
